IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ucta-nouns`
IMPORT `ucta-logic`

-- Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation.
-- LAYER 1, MODULE 8: PART 1, LIABILITY ARISING FROM SALE OR SUPPLY OF GOODS, sections 5 to 7
-- ("Guarantee" of consumer goods; Sale and hire-purchase; Miscellaneous contracts under which goods pass).
--
-- Each function takes `Reach of a section` (the answer of `s 1(2) and (3) whether an exception takes the
-- section out of the case`, module ucta-p1-introductory).  Where a flat negative takes the section out of the
-- case ("an exception takes it out"), a function in the text's own polarity ("a requirement of reasonableness
-- applies") answers JUST FALSE; a function that asks whether the person CAN exclude, rely or be made to do
-- something answers NOTHING, because the Act then says nothing about whether they can.  Where the reach
-- "cannot be told", every one of them answers NOTHING.
--
-- Spelling decides the reasonableness sites (ruling QA, 2026-11-04):
--   * "cannot ... except in so far as the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness" (s 7(4)):
--     JUST FALSE if the term is not shown to be reasonable; NOTHING if it is shown reasonable;
--   * "can be excluded or restricted ... but only in so far as the term satisfies the requirement of
--     reasonableness" (ss 6(3), 7(3)): JUST TRUE if shown reasonable, JUST FALSE if not shown.
-- Section 11(5) puts the burden of showing reasonableness on the party who claims it, so `reasonable` is
-- read as "it is shown that the term satisfies the requirement": JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE shown not;
-- NOTHING nobody has shown it, which is treated like "not shown" (fork F13 in NOTES.md).
-- Ss 3, 4, 6 and 7 speak of "contract term" only: a notice is NOTHING there (a fork in NOTES.md).
--
-- READING A RESULT (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Section 5 - guarantee of consumer goods`

-- src:191 | (2) For these purposes —
-- src:193 | (a) goods are to be regarded as “in consumer use” when a
-- src:194 | person is using them, or has them in his possession for use,
-- src:195 | otherwise than exclusively for the purposes of a business;
-- src:196 | and
@ref s 5(2)(a) (src:191-196)
GIVEN `a person is using the goods, or has them in his possession for use, otherwise than exclusively for the purposes of a business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(2)(a) the goods are in consumer use` MEANS
    IF `a person is using the goods, or has them in his possession for use, otherwise than exclusively for the purposes of a business`
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "goods are to be regarded as 'in consumer use' when a person is using them, or has them in his possession for use, otherwise than exclusively for the purposes of a business"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; marginal reading for a lawyer, a failed "when" on a definition is the text's no): the goods are used exclusively for the purposes of a business
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:198 | (b) anything in writing is a guarantee if it contains or purports
-- src:199 | to contain some promise or assurance (however worded or
-- src:200 | presented) that defects will be made good by complete or
-- src:201 | partial replacement, or by repair, monetary compensation
-- src:202 | or otherwise.
@ref s 5(2)(b) (src:198-202)
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains or purports to contain some promise or assurance (however worded or presented) that defects will be made good by complete or partial replacement, or by repair, monetary compensation or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(2)(b) the writing is a guarantee` MEANS
    IF `it is in writing` AND `it contains or purports to contain some promise or assurance (however worded or presented) that defects will be made good by complete or partial replacement, or by repair, monetary compensation or otherwise`
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "anything in writing is a guarantee if it contains or purports to contain some promise or assurance (however worded or presented) that defects will be made good by complete or partial replacement, or by repair, monetary compensation or otherwise"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; marginal reading for a lawyer, a failed "if" on a definition is the text's no): not in writing, or no such promise or assurance
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:204 | (3) This section does not apply as between the parties to a contract
-- src:205 | under or in pursuance of which possession or ownership of the goods
-- src:206 | passed.
@ref s 5(3) (src:204-206)
GIVEN `the parties are parties to a contract under or in pursuance of which possession or ownership of the goods passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3) section 5 applies as between the parties` MEANS
    IF `the parties are parties to a contract under or in pursuance of which possession or ownership of the goods passed`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply as between the parties to a contract under or in pursuance of which possession or ownership of the goods passed"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) disapplies the section only as between those parties
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:177 | 5.—(1) In the case of goods of a type ordinarily supplied for private
-- src:178 | use or consumption, where loss or damage —
-- src:180 | (a) arises from the goods proving defective while in consumer
-- src:181 | use; and
-- src:183 | (b) results from the negligence of a person concerned in the
-- src:184 | manufacture or distribution of the goods,
-- src:186 | liability for the loss or damage cannot be excluded or restricted by
-- src:187 | reference to any contract term or notice contained in or operating by
-- src:188 | reference to a guarantee of the goods.
@ref s 5(1) (src:177-188)
GIVEN `the goods are of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the goods were in consumer use` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the loss or damage arises from the goods proving defective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss or damage results from the negligence of a person concerned in the manufacture or distribution of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term or notice is contained in or operates by reference to a guarantee of the goods` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 5 applies as between the parties` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      reach IS A `Reach of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (reach EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 1(2) and (3) take the section out of the case, or whether they do cannot be told
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `section 5 applies as between the parties` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) says the section "does not apply as between the parties to a contract under or in pursuance of which possession or ownership of the goods passed"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the goods are of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of goods of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption"; whether they are is not shown
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the goods were in consumer use` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (a), "while in consumer use" (subsection (2)(a))
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the loss or damage arises from the goods proving defective` AND `the loss or damage results from the negligence of a person concerned in the manufacture or distribution of the goods`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limbs (a) "arises from the goods proving defective" and (b) "results from the negligence of a person concerned in the manufacture or distribution of the goods"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the term or notice is contained in or operates by reference to a guarantee of the goods` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any contract term or notice contained in or operating by reference to a guarantee of the goods" (subsection (2)(b))
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "liability for the loss or damage cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any contract term or notice contained in or operating by reference to a guarantee of the goods"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:177 | 5.—(1) In the case of goods of a type ordinarily supplied for private
-- src:178 | use or consumption, where loss or damage —
-- src:180 | (a) arises from the goods proving defective while in consumer
-- src:181 | use; and
-- src:183 | (b) results from the negligence of a person concerned in the
-- src:184 | manufacture or distribution of the goods,
-- src:186 | liability for the loss or damage cannot be excluded or restricted by
-- src:187 | reference to any contract term or notice contained in or operating by
-- src:188 | reference to a guarantee of the goods.
@ref s 5(1), the bar applies (src:177-188)
GIVEN `the goods are of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the goods were in consumer use` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the loss or damage arises from the goods proving defective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss or damage results from the negligence of a person concerned in the manufacture or distribution of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term or notice is contained in or operates by reference to a guarantee of the goods` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 5 applies as between the parties` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      reach IS A `Reach of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1) liability for the loss or damage cannot be excluded or restricted by a term or notice in a guarantee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF reach EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a flat negative takes the section out of the case -- section 1(3), sections 2 to 7 apply "only to business liability"; or a Part 3 provision -- so the bar does not apply
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (reach EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): whether section 1(2) and (3) or Part 3 take the section out of the case cannot be told
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `section 5 applies as between the parties` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (3), "This section does not apply as between the parties to a contract under or in pursuance of which possession or ownership of the goods passed" -- so the bar does not apply
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`the goods are of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of goods of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption" is a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)); whether the goods are of that type is not shown
        THEN NOTHING
        IF (`the goods were in consumer use` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the loss or damage arises from the goods proving defective`) OR (NOT `the loss or damage results from the negligence of a person concerned in the manufacture or distribution of the goods`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; marginal reading for a lawyer, a failed "where" on a negative statement is the text's no, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "where loss or damage (a) arises from the goods proving defective while in consumer use; and (b) results from the negligence of a person concerned in the manufacture or distribution of the goods" -- limb (a) or limb (b) fails, so the bar does not apply
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`the goods were in consumer use` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the goods were in consumer use (subsection (2)(a)) is not given
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the term or notice is contained in or operates by reference to a guarantee of the goods` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any contract term or notice contained in or operating by reference to a guarantee of the goods" describes the subject (subsection (2)(b)); not shown
        THEN NOTHING
        -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "liability for the loss or damage cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any contract term or notice contained in or operating by reference to a guarantee of the goods"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 6 - sale and hire-purchase`

-- src:242 | (4) The liabilities referred to in this section are not only the business
-- src:243 | liabilities defined by section 1(3), but include those arising under any
-- src:244 | contract of sale of goods or hire-purchase agreement.
@ref s 6(4) (src:242-244)
GIVEN `the liability is business liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of contract`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(4) the liability is one referred to in section 6` MEANS
    IF `the liability is business liability` OR kind EQUALS `A contract of sale of goods` OR kind EQUALS `A hire-purchase agreement`
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "The liabilities referred to in this section are not only the business liabilities defined by section 1(3), but include those arising under any contract of sale of goods or hire-purchase agreement"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include" -- the subsection names business liabilities and those under a sale or hire-purchase; section 1(3) then confines sections 2 to 7 "only to business liability" (see the reach aggregator, which takes the case out)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:210 | 6.—(1) Liability for breach of the obligations arising from —
-- src:212 | (a) section 12 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 (seller’s implied
-- src:213 | undertakings as to title, etc.); or
-- src:215 | (b) section 6 of the Hire-Purchase Act 1969 (the
-- src:216 | corresponding thing in relation to hire-purchase),
-- src:218 | cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any contract term.
@ref s 6(1) (src:210-218)
GIVEN obligation IS A `Obligation in a sale or hire-purchase`
      relied IS A `What is relied on`
      reach IS A `Reach of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the title provisions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (reach EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 1(2) and (3) take the section out of the case, or whether they do cannot be told
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (obligation EQUALS `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 12` OR obligation EQUALS `Hire-Purchase Act 1969 section 6`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) names section 12 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 and section 6 of the Hire-Purchase Act 1969
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (relied EQUALS `A contract term`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reference to any contract term"; a notice is not named (a notice having contractual effect is a fork in NOTES.md)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Liability for breach of the obligations arising from (a) section 12 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 ...; or (b) section 6 of the Hire-Purchase Act 1969 ..., cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any contract term"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:220 | (2) As against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of
-- src:221 | the obligations arising from —
-- src:223 | (a) section 13, 14 or 15 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 (seller’s
-- src:224 | implied undertakings as to conformity of goods with
-- src:225 | description or sample, or as to their quality or fitness for a
-- src:226 | particular purpose); or
-- src:228 | (b) section 6A, 6B or 6C of the Hire-Purchase Act 1969 (the
-- src:229 | corresponding things in relation to hire-purchase),
-- src:231 | cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any contract term.
@ref s 6(2) (src:220-231)
GIVEN consumer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      obligation IS A `Obligation in a sale or hire-purchase`
      relied IS A `What is relied on`
      reach IS A `Reach of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (reach EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 1(2) and (3) take the section out of the case, or whether they do cannot be told
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (consumer EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "As against a person dealing as consumer"; section 12 says whether the person deals as consumer
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (obligation EQUALS `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` OR obligation EQUALS `Hire-Purchase Act 1969 section 6A, 6B or 6C`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) names sections 13, 14 and 15 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 and sections 6A, 6B and 6C of the Hire-Purchase Act 1969
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (relied EQUALS `A contract term`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reference to any contract term"; a notice is not named (a notice having contractual effect is a fork in NOTES.md)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from (a) section 13, 14 or 15 ...; or (b) section 6A, 6B or 6C ..., cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any contract term"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:233 | (3) As against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the
-- src:234 | liability specified in subsection (2) can be excluded or restricted by
-- src:236 | 31.12.2021
-- src:237 | 6 Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 2020 Ed.
-- src:239 | reference to a contract term, but only in so far as the term satisfies the
-- src:240 | requirement of reasonableness.
@ref s 6(3), the requirement applies (src:233-240)
GIVEN consumer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      obligation IS A `Obligation in a sale or hire-purchase`
      relied IS A `What is relied on`
      reach IS A `Reach of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF reach EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a flat negative takes the section out of the case -- section 1(3), sections 2 to 7 apply "only to business liability"; the First Schedule, "do not extend to"; or a Part 3 provision ("do not apply", "are not subject to", "do not operate", "is not precluded", "Nothing in this Act applies") -- so no requirement of reasonableness applies under this section
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (reach EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): whether section 1(2) and (3), the First Schedule or Part 3 take the section out of the case cannot be told (whether the person protected deals as consumer is not known and the answers differ, or an input outside the text decides it)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (consumer EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "As against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer"; section 12 says whether the person deals as consumer
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (obligation EQUALS `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` OR obligation EQUALS `Hire-Purchase Act 1969 section 6A, 6B or 6C`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the liability specified in subsection (2)"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (relied EQUALS `A contract term`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reference to a contract term"; a notice is not named (a notice having contractual effect is a fork in NOTES.md)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "can be excluded or restricted by reference to a contract term, but only in so far as the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:233 | (3) As against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the
-- src:234 | liability specified in subsection (2) can be excluded or restricted by
-- src:236 | 31.12.2021
-- src:237 | 6 Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 2020 Ed.
-- src:239 | reference to a contract term, but only in so far as the term satisfies the
-- src:240 | requirement of reasonableness.
@ref s 6(3) (src:233-240)
GIVEN consumer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      obligation IS A `Obligation in a sale or hire-purchase`
      relied IS A `What is relied on`
      reasonable IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      reach IS A `Reach of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability specified in subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` consumer obligation relied reach EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) does not reach this case, or the section is taken out of the case (the twin `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` answers that)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF reasonable EQUALS JUST TRUE
        -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "can be excluded or restricted by reference to a contract term, but only in so far as the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness" -- the term is shown to satisfy it
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only in so far as the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness" -- the term is not shown to satisfy it (unreasonable, or reasonableness not shown): it is for those claiming that it does to show that it does (s 11(5))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

GIVEN consumer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      obligation IS A `Obligation in a sale or hire-purchase`
      relied IS A `What is relied on`
      reasonable IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      reach IS A `Reach of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` MEANS
    CONSIDER consumer
    -- Consumer status is given: section 6(2) if consumer, section 6(3) if not.
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF x
        THEN `s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` consumer obligation relied reach
        ELSE `s 6(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability specified in subsection (2)` consumer obligation relied reasonable reach
    -- Consumer status is not given: the two subsections give the same answer only if the term is not shown reasonable (both are then JUST FALSE, fork F13).
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST TRUE) obligation relied reach
            EQUALS `s 6(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability specified in subsection (2)` (JUST FALSE) obligation relied reasonable reach
        THEN `s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST TRUE) obligation relied reach
        ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 7 - miscellaneous contracts under which goods pass`

-- src:248 | 7.—(1) Where the possession or ownership of goods passes under
-- src:249 | or in pursuance of a contract not governed by the law of sale of goods
-- src:250 | or hire-purchase, subsections (2) to (4) apply as regards the effect (if
-- src:251 | any) to be given to contract terms excluding or restricting liability for
-- src:252 | breach of obligation arising by implication of law from the nature of
-- src:253 | the contract.
@ref s 7(1) (src:248-253)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of contract`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) subsections (2) to (4) apply` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `A contract, not of sale of goods or hire-purchase, under which possession or ownership of goods passes`
    -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "Where the possession or ownership of goods passes under or in pursuance of a contract not governed by the law of sale of goods or hire-purchase, subsections (2) to (4) apply"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; marginal reading for a lawyer, a failed "where" on a positive statement of application is the text's no): the contract is a sale, hire-purchase or one under which no goods pass
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:255 | (2) As against a person dealing as consumer, liability in respect of
-- src:256 | the goods’ correspondence with description or sample, or their
-- src:257 | quality or fitness for any particular purpose, cannot be excluded or
-- src:258 | restricted by reference to any such term.
@ref s 7(2) (src:255-258)
GIVEN `subsections (2) to (4) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      consumer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      obligation IS A `Obligation in another goods contract`
      relied IS A `What is relied on`
      reach IS A `Reach of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (reach EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 1(2) and (3) and the First Schedule take the section out of the case, or whether they do cannot be told
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`subsections (2) to (4) apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1), "Where the possession or ownership of goods passes under or in pursuance of a contract not governed by the law of sale of goods or hire-purchase"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (consumer EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "As against a person dealing as consumer"; section 12 says whether the person deals as consumer
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (obligation EQUALS `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` OR obligation EQUALS `Quality or fitness of the goods for a particular purpose`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) names "the goods' correspondence with description or sample, or their quality or fitness for any particular purpose"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (relied EQUALS `A contract term`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reference to any such term" (a contract term, subsection (1)); a notice is not named (a notice having contractual effect is a fork in NOTES.md)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "As against a person dealing as consumer, liability in respect of the goods' correspondence with description or sample, or their quality or fitness for any particular purpose, cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any such term"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:260 | (3) As against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, that
-- src:261 | liability can be excluded or restricted by reference to such a term, but
-- src:262 | only in so far as the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness.
@ref s 7(3), the requirement applies (src:260-262)
GIVEN `subsections (2) to (4) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      consumer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      obligation IS A `Obligation in another goods contract`
      relied IS A `What is relied on`
      reach IS A `Reach of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF reach EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a flat negative takes the section out of the case -- section 1(3), sections 2 to 7 apply "only to business liability"; the First Schedule, "do not extend to"; or a Part 3 provision ("do not apply", "are not subject to", "do not operate", "is not precluded", "Nothing in this Act applies") -- so no requirement of reasonableness applies under this section
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (reach EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): whether section 1(2) and (3), the First Schedule or Part 3 take the section out of the case cannot be told (whether the person protected deals as consumer is not known and the answers differ, or an input outside the text decides it)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`subsections (2) to (4) apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (consumer EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "As against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer"; section 12 says whether the person deals as consumer
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (obligation EQUALS `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` OR obligation EQUALS `Quality or fitness of the goods for a particular purpose`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that liability", the liability in subsection (2)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (relied EQUALS `A contract term`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reference to such a term"; a notice is not named (a notice having contractual effect is a fork in NOTES.md)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "can be excluded or restricted by reference to such a term, but only in so far as the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:260 | (3) As against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, that
-- src:261 | liability can be excluded or restricted by reference to such a term, but
