        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`subsections (2) to (4) apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such term" refers to the terms of subsection (1)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (obligation EQUALS `Supply of Goods Act 1982 section 2 (implied terms about title)`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3A) names section 2 of the Supply of Goods Act 1982
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (relied EQUALS `A contract term`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reference to any such term"; a notice is not named (a notice having contractual effect is a fork in NOTES.md)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Liability for breach of the obligations arising under section 2 of the Supply of Goods Act 1982 ... cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any such term"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:271 | (4) Liability in respect of —
-- src:273 | (a) the right to transfer ownership of the goods, or give
-- src:274 | possession; or
-- src:276 | (b) the assurance of quiet possession to a person taking goods
-- src:277 | in pursuance of the contract,
-- src:279 | cannot (in a case to which subsection (3A) does not apply) be
-- src:280 | excluded or restricted by reference to any such term except in so far as
-- src:281 | the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness.
@ref s 7(4), the requirement applies (src:271-281)
GIVEN `subsections (2) to (4) apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      obligation IS A `Obligation in another goods contract`
      `subsection (3A) applies to the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      relied IS A `What is relied on`
      reach IS A `Reach of a section`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(4) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF reach EQUALS `An exception takes the section out of the case`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a flat negative takes the section out of the case -- section 1(3), sections 2 to 7 apply "only to business liability"; the First Schedule, "do not extend to"; or a Part 3 provision ("do not apply", "are not subject to", "do not operate", "is not precluded", "Nothing in this Act applies") -- so no requirement of reasonableness applies under this section
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (reach EQUALS `No exception takes the section out of the case`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): whether section 1(2) and (3), the First Schedule or Part 3 take the section out of the case cannot be told (whether the person protected deals as consumer is not known and the answers differ, or an input outside the text decides it)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`subsections (2) to (4) apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such term" refers to the terms of subsection (1)
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (obligation EQUALS `The right to transfer ownership of the goods, or give possession` OR obligation EQUALS `The assurance of quiet possession to a person taking the goods`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) names (a) the right to transfer ownership of the goods, or give possession, and (b) the assurance of quiet possession
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `subsection (3A) applies to the case`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(in a case to which subsection (3A) does not apply)"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (relied EQUALS `A contract term`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reference to any such term"; a notice is not named (a notice having contractual effect is a fork in NOTES.md)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- TRUE-kind (the text says yes in its own words): "except in so far as the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

